Restore the current CIX manager-5/V3 allocation ABI without importing the
vendor driver's private IOMMU allocator.

Reserve four standard DMA-owned 3 GiB IOVA pools, report their dynamically
allocated bases as ASIDs, and give each file-owned exec_id a suballocated
arena.  Implement P1 allocation modes 1--3, exact P1 whole-arena free
semantics, transactional REBIND, fragmented page linking, and segment-aware
cache maintenance.  Ordinary mode-0 allocation retains its proven low DMA
window; the device's wider DMA mask is used only for the ASID pools.

Enable ASID arenas by default after verified inference completed on O6
through every ASID.  Retain the read-only, load-time v3_asid_arenas
parameter so that N selects the safe single-ASID path for recovery or
diagnosis.  Mode 4 is a separate Sky1-lineage extension and is not enabled
here.

Source: ABI and manager-5 behaviour from CIX NPU driver
p1_7.0_v6.2.0 (commit 93a0698fc00d848afefc8e33022d2a2878663677),
using the standard Linux DMA IOVA API rather than the vendor implementation.

